Citrix NetScaler Threat Hunt — Detections & Search Reference
Hunt: ORG WPaaS Downstream Session Hijacking & Replay Audit CVEs: CVE-2026-88771 (pre-auth command injection / log poisoning) · CVE-2026-88772 (DTLS overflow RCE/DoS) Sprint: October 2026 · Mindset: assume-breach Last updated: 2026-10-01

Conventions (unchanged across all searches)
	• Splunk index placeholder: <your_citrix_index>
	• Sourcetype for appliance syslog + config audit: citrix:netscaler:syslog
	• WPaaS egress CIDRs: <your_WPAAS_CIDR_range> (test range) and <your_WPAAS_CIDR_range_2> (tenant apps/desktops). Both go in every origin-classification cidrmatch OR-set.
	• Origin classification: inside either CIDR = internal; else external.
	• Settled during scoping: no duplicate ingestion; src_ip extraction clean (no leading space); config-audit events (CMD_EXECUTED) confirmed present in this index/sourcetype on both in-scope gateways.
	• Pin latest to a fixed timestamp for any figure you cite. Relative/live windows drift the counts by single digits.
	• Validate before trusting any new field: confirm it populates in the real sourcetype (existing ≠ populated); a misspelled/absent field resolves to null and silently empties results.

