S1 — Baseline Delivery Sweep (CVE-2026-88771)
Confirms and quantifies injection delivery. Anchors on the structural marker "pitboss PPE" NSPPE (not the crash phrase, which tokenizes inconsistently). Handles both AAA formats, URL-encoded payloads, truncated lines, and separates zero-day vs post-disclosure waves.
index=<your_citrix_index> ("pitboss PPE" OR "pitboss%20PPE") NSPPE earliest="09/01/2026:00:00:00" latest="10/01/2026:23:59:59"
| rex field=_raw "(?:login claims for user|parsed data; username:) <(?<payload>pitboss PPE.+?)>(?:,? pwdlen| with configured schema)"
| rex field=_raw "(?:login|User-Agent)[=:]\s?(?<payload2>pitboss(?:%20| )PPE.+?)(?:&(?:passwd|pwd)|&nsg|\r|$)"
| eval payload=coalesce(payload,payload2)
| eval payload=if(match(payload,"%[0-9A-Fa-f]{2}"),urldecode(payload),payload)
| eval has_terminator=if(match(_raw,"pitboss PPE.+?>"),1,0)
| eval delivery=case(isnotnull(payload),"parsed",
                     match(_raw,"%20PPE|%3B|%24%7BIFS%7D"),"encoded_http_log",
                     has_terminator=0,"truncated_no_payload",
                     true(),"unparsed_NEW_FORMAT")
| eval payload=coalesce(payload,"__".delivery."__")
| eval wave=if(_time>=strptime("2026-09-27","%Y-%m-%d"),"post_disclosure","zero_day")
| stats count min(_time) as first max(_time) as last values(host) as gateways dc(host) as hosts by payload delivery wave
| convert timeformat="%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z" ctime(first) ctime(last)
| sort wave first
Reading: unparsed_NEW_FORMAT > 0 = a delivery path not yet parsed (pull a sample, build a rex). truncated_no_payload = operator ns.log ask (long stagers cut at ~185-byte syslog limit; stage-2 URL survives only in the appliance's local log). wave separates the 9/12 zero-day actor from the post-disclosure flood.
Notes: Report counts as a floor, not false-precise. For alerting, save a per-event copy (drop stats, trigger on any result).

S2 — IOC Pull
Extracts what each payload intended to reach/do, grouped by indicator. No-callback payloads self-label into technique buckets rather than collapsing into one opaque row. IOCs here are delivery-side (intent); they become execution proof only when appliance egress shows the gateway actually connected.
index=<your_citrix_index> ("pitboss PPE" OR "pitboss%20PPE") NSPPE earliest="09/01/2026:00:00:00" latest="10/01/2026:23:59:59"
| rex field=_raw "(?:login claims for user|parsed data; username:) <(?<payload>pitboss PPE.+?)>(?:,? pwdlen| with configured schema)"
| rex field=_raw "(?:login|User-Agent)[=:]\s?(?<payload2>pitboss(?:%20| )PPE.+?)(?:&(?:passwd|pwd)|&nsg|\r|$)"
| eval payload=coalesce(payload,payload2)
| eval payload=if(match(payload,"%[0-9A-Fa-f]{2}"),urldecode(payload),payload)
| where isnotnull(payload)
| rex field=payload "(?<url>https?://[^\s'\"]+)"
| rex field=payload "(?<oast>[a-z0-9][a-z0-9.-]*\.(?:oast\.(?:fun|pro|site|live|me)|interactsh\.com|burpcollaborator\.net|dnslog\.cn|dnsl\.cc|requestbin\.net|pipedream\.net|canarytokens\.com))"
| rex field=payload "(?:curl|wget|fetch|nslookup|dig|host|nc|ncat|telnet)\s+(?:-{1,2}[a-zA-Z][\w-]*(?:[= ]\S+)?\s+)*(?<cb_host>[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9.-]+\.[a-zA-Z]{2,})"
| rex field=payload "(?<gsocket_secret>\b[a-f0-9]{32}\b)"
| rex field=payload "(?<deaddrop_tag>\b(?:C3|KP):)"
| rex field=payload "(?<marker>nx_verify\.html|admin_ui/log\.txt|\.ctxs\.receiver|xua\.html|insight-new\.js)"
| rex field=payload "(?<file_ioc>/(?:var|netscaler|flash|usr)/[^\s'\";|>]+)"
| rex field=payload "(?:^|;|\|)\s*(?<cmd_ioc>(?:id|whoami|uname|hostname|cat|chmod|tar|nc|ncat)\b[^;|]*)"
| eval net_ioc=case(
    isnotnull(url),url,
    isnotnull(oast),oast,
    isnotnull(cb_host),cb_host,
    match(payload,"\bz?grep\b.{0,15}/var/log"),"__DEADDROP_logfile__",
    match(payload,"\|\s?php\b"),"__DEADDROP_php__",
    isnotnull(deaddrop_tag),"__DEADDROP_tag__",
    isnotnull(marker),"__MARKER_only__",
    match(payload,"\bid\b|whoami"),"__RECON_only__",
    true(),"__NO_IOC_UNCLASSIFIED__")
| eval ioc_display=coalesce(url, oast, cb_host, file_ioc, cmd_ioc, "__NEEDS_REVIEW__")
| rex max_match=0 field=net_ioc "(?<embedded_ip>\b(?:\d{1,3}\.){3}\d{1,3}\b)"
| eval exfil_flag=if((isnotnull(url) AND (match(url,"\?\S*=\S") OR match(url,"://[^/]+/\w+/\S"))),"EXFIL_SHAPE_review",null())
| eval technique=mvappend(
    case(match(payload,"--no-verify-(peer|hostname)"),"tls_bypass"),
    case(match(payload,"\$\{?IFS\}?"),"ifs_evasion"),
    case(match(payload,"\bz?grep\b.{0,15}/var/log"),"logfile_deaddrop"),
    case(match(payload,"\|\s?php\b"),"php_stage2"),
    case(match(payload,"\bnc\s+\S+\s+\d+\s+-e"),"reverse_shell"),
    case(match(payload,"\bpython\S*\s+/var|\.py\b"),"python_stager"),
    case(isnotnull(gsocket_secret),"gsocket:".gsocket_secret),
    case(isnotnull(deaddrop_tag),"log_deaddrop_tag"),
    case(isnotnull(marker),"marker_write:".marker))
| eval wave=if(_time>=strptime("2026-09-27","%Y-%m-%d"),"post_disclosure","zero_day")
| stats count min(_time) as first max(_time) as last dc(payload) as distinct_payloads values(net_ioc) as bucket values(embedded_ip) as embedded_ips values(exfil_flag) as exfil values(technique) as techniques dc(host) as hosts values(host) as gateways by ioc_display wave
| convert timeformat="%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z" ctime(first) ctime(last)
| sort - count

Reading: exfil populated = callback carrying data (priority). ioc_display=__NEEDS_REVIEW__ = nothing extracted (hand-review pile; should be tiny). Observed result: zero-day bucket resolved to a single PHP dead-drop shape (zgrep$IFS … /var/log/*s-* | b64decode | php), 1 distinct payload, ~2,096 events — one actor/one payload, not a blind spot.


